{
  "title": "That's My Atypical Girl",
  "description": "Yokoi is a manga artist who spends his nights delivering newspapers just to make rent, since his original works just don’t seem to sell. Suddenly, one day he gets a visit from Saito-san, a self-proclaimed fan of Yokoi’s work who made the long journey to meet him. Yokoi quickly realizes that the things Saito-san sees, feels, and thinks about are different from most people… These two struggle together to find a place to belong in this unique slice-of-life! \n\n(Source: Kodansha USA) \n\n*Note: Original serialization ran for 123 chapters. These were then combined to make up 100 chapters in the volume releases.*\n\nStatus: completed\nTags: 21st century, Abusive Father, Animal Cruelty, Depression, Drama, Drawing, Dropout, Erotic Novelist, Estranged Family, Japan, Male Protagonist, Philosophy, Poor Protagonist, Psychological, Psychosexual, Romance, Seinen, Slice of Life, Studious Character, Writing, Abusive Family Member, Autism, Bullying, Cohabitation, Comic Artist, Disability, Female Lead, Female Protagonist, Flashbacks, Glasses-Wearing Female Lead, Heterosexual, Language Barrier, Loner Protagonist, Male Lead, Mangaka in a Manga, Mental Illness, Primarily Adult Cast, Rehabilitation, Self-Harm, Suicidal Character, Writers, Erotic Mangaka, Past Plays a Big Role, Tragedy, Violent Female Lead",
  "artist": "Renji Morita",
